      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Never holding the key in the Hub\u0027s own environment** \u2014 The Hub process itself does not store the credential in its environment variables.\n\n2. **Local secrets loader at startup** \u2014 A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file when the system starts up.\n\n3. **Injection into child processes only** \u2014 The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start, without ever being written to or inherited from the Hub\u0027s environment.\n\n4. **Isolation benefit** \u2014 This means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 2549,
      "output_tokens": 208
    }
